      "game_seq": 436,
      "reasoning": "Turn 8! Board is looking incredible. I have a 6/6 flying Reaper from the Abyss and a 5/5 Morkrut Banshee, both ready to attack. Opponent has just Fertilid (2/2) and is at 11 life. \n\
\n\
Let me play a Swamp for the land drop, then deploy Liliana's Steward for 1 mana. Steward can sacrifice to make opponent discard - useful utility. Then attack with everything for 11 (6+5) which is exactly lethal if they don't block!\n\
\n\
Wait - Reaper has flying, so Fertilid can't block it. If they block Banshee with Fertilid, that's 5 damage from Reaper + 0 from Banshee (blocked) = 5 damage. But Fertilid dies, triggering Reaper's morbid at end step... though nothing left to destroy.\n\
\n\
If they don't block at all: 6 + 5 = 11, exactly their life total. That's lethal!\n\
\n\
Let me play Swamp first, then Liliana's Steward, then attack.",
